{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773940483,"nonce":"Y+kWgbMQ83hbIwAdL617YQM6J1A=","title":"Markdown formatting in sidebar elements: headings and truncation","message":"Sidebar elements (inbox items, issue titles, chat log titles, etc.) render simple Markdown, which is generally good. Two issues with the current behavior:\n\n1. **Headings should not be rendered.** Markdown headings (e.g. `# Foo`) should not change text size or add whitespace in sidebar contexts. Only inline formatting should be rendered: bold, italic, monospace, strikethrough, etc.\n\n2. **Truncation breaks inline Markdown fencing.** When a title contains a backtick-fenced path (e.g. `/some/long/path/to/file.ts`) and the title is truncated for sidebar display, the truncation happens on the raw Markdown string before formatting. This produces visible Markdown syntax artifacts — e.g. a lone opening backtick followed by plain-text path fragment.","files":null}]}